sequenceDiagram
    actor Receptionist
    participant API as API process
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Relay as OutboxRelayService
    participant Redis
    participant GW as QueueGateway
    participant Web as Web app
    Receptionist->>API: Queue action, for example check-in
    API->>DB: BEGIN, lock the queue session row, update the entry
    API->>DB: INSERT queue_events and 3 outbox rows, pg_notify queue_outbox
    API->>DB: COMMIT
    API-->>Receptionist: success response
    DB-->>Relay: NOTIFY queue_outbox, or the 1 second poll
    Relay->>DB: SELECT unpublished outbox rows FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED, max 100
    Relay->>Redis: PUBLISH each row on the realtime channel
    Redis-->>Relay: accepted
    Relay->>DB: UPDATE outbox SET published_at, COMMIT
    Redis-->>GW: message reaches every API instance
    GW->>Web: emit queue.event to session and board rooms, display.event to the display room
    Web->>API: newer seq, so refetch the screen snapshot
    Note over Relay,GW: Worker heartbeat every 5 s. Without a heartbeat for 15 s an API instance refuses sockets and clients poll.
